# Panel 253's R6 (2026-11-19): the catalogue's entry `kit` lists `csv` alone,
# so `csv` and the module it uses, `text`, are the program's; `flags` is in
# the same folder and not listed, and its `use` is refused, told once with
# the command that lists it in a note, never as a `Fix`, the catalogue being
# no file of the compilation.
use <kit>/csv
use <kit>/flags  #~ package_not_listed

function main()
    print(csv.first("a,b"))
    print(flags.on())
